menu "T-Deck MAX Phone"

    config TDECK_MAX_SIM_MODE
        bool "Simulation mode (skip real I2C/SPI transactions)"
        default n
        help
            QEMU has no peripheral models for this board's XL9555 I/O
            expander, ES8311 codec, TCA8418 keypad, or GDEQ031T10 e-paper
            display -- real I2C/SPI transactions to them just time out.
            Enable this only for QEMU/host boot-testing of the non-hardware
            logic (Wi-Fi, SIP UAC, app orchestration): hardware init calls
            log and return ESP_OK without touching the bus. Never enable
            for a real hardware build -- the device would boot silently
            "successful" while nothing is actually initialized.

    config TDECK_MAX_KEYPAD_DEBUG
        bool "Log raw TCA8418 key events"
        default n
        help
            Log the raw event byte, decoded key_num, and resulting row/col
            for every keypress. The row/col decode and keymap are inherited
            from LilyGO's example and not yet verified on hardware; enable
            this during bench bring-up to derive the real map empirically,
            then turn it back off (it logs on every keypress).

    config TDECK_MAX_HALT_ON_INIT_FAIL
        bool "Abort boot if a peripheral fails to initialize"
        default n
        help
            When disabled (the default), a peripheral that fails to come up
            is logged and boot continues, so the serial log reports every
            failure and the I2C scan still runs. When enabled, the first
            failure aborts.

            Default is off deliberately: fail-fast during bring-up gives a
            panic-reboot loop with no UI and no indication of WHICH device
            NAKed, which is the least debuggable outcome on a board with
            six devices sharing one I2C bus.

endmenu
